<title>PORTUGAL: Escudo rock steady after Bank/Portugal rate cut.</title>
<headline>Escudo rock steady after Bank/Portugal rate cut.</headline>
<dateline>LISBON 1997-07-11</dateline>
<text>
<p>The escudo continued to trade steady against the mark despite a Bank of Portugal rate cut which took most analysts by surprise.</p>
<p>The escudo was trading at 100.87/90 to the mark against 100.95/98 at the opening.</p>
<p>&quot;The escudo is calm (showing) no reaction to the cut in Bank of Portugal rates,&quot; said one trader. &quot;Any reaction on the part of the escudo will be to the pound and the dollar in line with other European currencies,&quot; he said.</p>
<p>--Lisbon bureau 3511-3150035</p>
</text>
